// Detection: Password spray against Windows hosts
// MITRE: T1110.003 Password Spraying
// Data source: SecurityEvent (EventID 4625), via Windows Security Events (AMA) on the DC
// Engine: Microsoft Sentinel scheduled analytics rule
// Logic: one source IP failing against MANY distinct accounts (spray), vs 007's many-passwords-one-account (brute force).
// Tuning: threshold >= 5 distinct accounts, not 2 — shared gateways/jump hosts can produce a couple of failed accounts innocently.
// Investigate: check for a 4624 success from the same source, EXCLUDING ANONYMOUS LOGON and machine ($) accounts.
// Test: nxc smb <DC> -u users.txt -p OnePassword ; expect one row, DistinctAccounts = number sprayed.

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize DistinctAccounts = dcount(Account),
            AccountsTried    = make_set(Account),
            FailureCount     = count(),
            FirstSeen        = min(TimeGenerated),
            LastSeen         = max(TimeGenerated)
    by IpAddress, Computer
| where DistinctAccounts >= 5
| sort by DistinctAccounts desc
